-- title:
--   Pinned relabelling lifts to a residue-trivial automorphism of R
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q$ (with $q \neq 2$ and $5 \le q$) and $\ell$ (with $3 \le \ell$), a nonzero natural number $M'$, and a commutative base ring $A_0$ in which $\ell$ is invertible. Assume the two stability hypotheses `hℓ`: a level-$\ell$ datum $(x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ satisfying `IsLevelPStructure` for $W$ continues to satisfy it for $C \bullet W$ after the induced change of the coordinates, and `hM`: `IsGamma0PowAt` for $W$, $p$, $k$ and $h$ is preserved when $h$ is replaced by `kernelVariableChangeDeg` along $C$ in degree `gamma0PowDeg p k`. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a family of relative group laws on the projective models of curves with unit discriminant which is chord-tangent and has the origin as identity, and $\mathcal{T}$ a level transport for $\mathcal{G}$ and $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport`; assume also `hVC` and `hCO`, the existence of graded ring maps on the projective-model coordinate rings realising a variable change, respectively a coefficient homomorphism, each dominating the irrelevant ideal. These data assemble the rigid Weierstrass datum `rigidDataPow`, whose level structure is a triple consisting of kernel polynomials for the prime powers dividing $M'$, a level-$\ell$ datum, and a Drinfeld pair for $q$; let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the associated moduli datum, that is a ring $B_0$ over $A_0$ with a point `univ` over $B_0$ through which every point over every $A_0$-algebra factors uniquely, and let $x$ be a raw curve-with-level-structure over $B_0$ whose class is `univ`. Let $R$ be a noetherian local domain, complete for its maximal ideal, an algebra over $A_0$, with $\iota : B_0 \to R$ an $A_0$-algebra map; let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ in which $\ell$ and $M'$ are nonzero, and $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ a surjection with kernel the maximal ideal. Let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal generated by $q$ and residue surjection $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$, with $R$ a $W_0$-algebra compatibly over $A_0$ and $\mathrm{res}_R \circ (\text{structure map}) = \mathrm{res}_0$. Assume `hfac`: for every Artinian local $W_0$-algebra $T$ over $A_0$ with compatible residue surjection onto $k$ and every $A_0$-algebra map $\varphi : B_0 \to T$ reducing to $\mathrm{res}_R \circ \iota$, there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\Phi : R \to T$ with $\mathrm{res}_T \circ \Phi = \mathrm{res}_R$ and $\Phi \circ \iota = \varphi$. Finally let $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lie in $\Gamma_0(M')$ and let $\rho_\gamma$ be an automorphism of the moduli problem (a functorial self-map of the point functor preserving $j$) which is pinned by $\gamma$ in the sense of `hpin`: over any field $T$ over $A_0$, if two raw objects $y,y'$ have the same curve and the same $\Gamma_0$-component, the level-$\ell$ datum of $y'$ is `LevelPData.relabel` of that of $y$ by the matrix $\gamma$, and the Drinfeld pair of $y'$ is `RawDrinfeldPair.relabel` of that of $y$ by $\gamma$ using $\mathcal{G}$ (the discriminant of the pair's curve being a unit), then $\rho_\gamma$ sends the class of $y$ to the class of $y'$. Assume `hfix`: writing $\rho_B = P_0.\mathrm{classify}(\rho_\gamma \cdot \mathrm{univ}) : B_0 \to B_0$ for the unique classifying map, $\iota(\rho_B b) - \iota(b)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R$ for all $b \in B_0$. The conclusion is that there exists a $W_0$-algebra automorphism $\theta_0$ of $R$ with $\theta_0(\iota(b)) = \iota(\rho_B b)$ for all $b \in B_0$, and with $\theta_0(r) - r$ in the maximal ideal for every $r \in R$.
--
--   This transports a $\Gamma_0(M')$-relabelling automorphism of the full-level moduli problem, pinned on field-valued points by a matrix $\gamma$ and fixing the closed point cut out by $\iota$, to an automorphism of the complete local ring $R$ over the coefficient ring $W_0$ which is trivial on the residue field. It is used in the analysis of the induced action on the formal parameter at the origin, where the resulting automorphism of $R$ is compared with its linear part.
